The Apache-2.0 traffic files are identified by their SPDX headers in
pkg/traffic, pkg/monitor/traffic*.go, cmd/agent/traffic*.go and
model/traffic_test.go. Traffic additions adapted from that implementation
in cmd/agent/main.go, model/config.go and pkg/monitor/network.go retain
Apache-2.0 terms alongside the current upstream code in those files.

The port integrates the traffic policy with the current runtime snapshots,
reuses the current hostfs persistence operations, and keeps network rates
in raw bytes per second in both report modes. The configuration editor and
update config snapshot were adapted on the current upstream baseline for
local policy protection. docs/traffic.md describes the public configuration
and operation of this port.
